{
    // markdownlint-cli2 ran on defaults, which meant MD013 (80-column lines) against a
    // corpus written one-line-per-paragraph from its first page. That is a deliberate
    // authoring style, not a backlog: an edit to a sentence produces a one-line diff
    // instead of reflowing a whole paragraph, which is what keeps a docs review readable.
    // The result was 529 of 532 errors being the linter disagreeing with the house style,
    // and the three REAL defects buried underneath - a dead link fragment, a trailing
    // space, and a wrapped em-dash that markdown was rendering as a stray bullet. A gate
    // nobody can read is a gate nobody runs, which is why this one had been red for its
    // whole life and never made it into CI.
    //
    // So MD013 is off, deliberately, and every other rule stays on and stays green.
    // Rendered line length is the browser's job here: Starlight sets the measure.
    // Rules only - the lint:md script owns which files are linted.
    "config": {
        "MD013": false
    }
}
